{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeLiftInterface"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.equal_split_of_naturality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.equal_split_of_naturality","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeNaturality.lean#L90-L97","doc":"**Trace shadow of the naturality square.** The forward square is strictly\nstronger than the `equal_split` trace identity: summing the diagonal of the\nsquare (with the hermiticity of `W`) recovers `Wbar.trace = W.trace`. This\nrecords that `equal_split` is the shadow of `rho_intertwines_weight`, closing\nthe loop with `TauRhoHodgeLiftInterface`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.rho_intertwines_weight_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.rho_intertwines_weight_symm","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeNaturality.lean#L79-L88","doc":"**The reverse square.** Applying the forward square to `star v` and using the\n`star`-involution recovers the `Wbar`-to-`W` direction:\n`star (Wbar.mulVec v) = W.mulVec (star v)`. Together with\n`rho_intertwines_weight` this is the full two-sided naturality of `ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.rho_intertwines_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.rho_intertwines_weight","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeNaturality.lean#L65-L77","doc":"**The ρ-naturality square, conditional on the B2 lift.** Given\n`[TauRhoHodgeLift g W Wbar]`, entrywise conjugation `ρ = star` intertwines the\n`H^{1,0}` weight `W` with the `H^{0,1}` weight `Wbar`:\n\n  `star (W.mulVec v) = Wbar.mulVec (star v)`   for every mode `v`.\n\nThis is the commuting square asserting that `τ` carries the fibre reality\nstructure `ρ` to Hodge conjugation *naturally*. Derived from the lift's\n`conjugated` field alone. OPEN modulo the class (no instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.star_mulVec_map_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeNaturality.star_mulVec_map_star","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeNaturality.lean#L54-L63","doc":"**The ρ-naturality square (forward), general form.** For any matrix `W` and\nits entrywise conjugate `W.map (starRingEnd ℂ)`, conjugation intertwines the two\nweight actions: `star (W.mulVec v) = (W.map conj).mulVec (star v)`. This is the\nmatrix-level naturality of `ρ = star`; it is `star`-linearity of `mulVec` and\nneeds no hypothesis on `W`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}